cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use ihwkit, please cite this software and the original IHW
  method paper (Ignatiadis et al. 2016). Cite Ignatiadis and Huber
  (2021) when discussing theoretical properties of cross-weighting.
  Cite the Bioconductor IHW R package when you use or compare against
  that implementation.
title: "ihwkit: Independent Hypothesis Weighting with NumPy"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/eneskemalergin/ihwkit"
authors:
  - family-names: Ergin
    given-names: Enes Kemal
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9810-7399"
keywords:
  - false discovery rate
  - independent hypothesis weighting
  - multiple testing
  - statistics
abstract: >
  ihwkit learns hypothesis weights from an informative covariate, then
  applies weighted Benjamini-Hochberg or Bonferroni adjustment. Version
  0.1 is a one-module, NumPy-only implementation of five-fold
  cross-weighting and the unregularized (infinite-lambda) allocation.
  It is not a replacement for the full Bioconductor IHW R package,
  which still provides regularization, nested lambda selection, and
  plotting.
